"Did your neighbors brag about their cool beta-decay powered nightlights?  Do"
" them one better!  The CuppaTech 4 radioisotope thermoelectric generator is "
"a three kilogram chunk of metal - mostly lead - with a slug of curium-244 "
"encased within.  It is capable of generating somewhere between 100-150 Watts"
" of thermal energy, although its electrical generation capacity is minimal "
"at only 2 Watts.  Careful!  Curium is great at making heat, and also "
"releases deadly gamma radiation.  Keep away from cellular life forms."
msgstr ""

